# What may enter an image layer. This is a security control, not build hygiene.
#
# **Deny everything, then re-admit by name.** The opposite order — listing what to
# exclude — fails silently the first time someone adds a file: a new credential, a
# new corpus directory or a new dump lands in the build context because nobody
# remembered to exclude it. With this order a new file is absent until it is named,
# and the failure mode is a broken build rather than a leaked document.
#
# Three things in this repository must never reach a layer, and all three are
# covered by the deny-all rather than by being listed:
#
#   .env                              PostgreSQL and object-store credentials
#   data/corpus/held_out_*            filings frozen for evaluation (§8). An image
#                                     is a distributable artefact, so held-out
#                                     documents inside one are held out of nothing
#   model_cache/                      506 MB of Docling artefacts no service here needs
#
# Note that a layer is permanent. Deleting a file in a later RUN does not remove it
# from the image, so "COPY then clean up" is not a mitigation.

*

# The application itself. Source rather than a wheel, because
# `persistence/database.py` resolves `migrations/` relative to its own __file__ and
# the installed-package layout breaks that derivation. See docker/api/Dockerfile.
!src/

# Schema history. The readiness probe compares the database revision against this
# directory, so an image that serves /health/ready has to carry it.
!migrations/
!alembic.ini

# Version metadata: `finsight.__version__` is read through this at build time.
!pyproject.toml

# The pinned version authority, plus the per-image direct dependency lists.
!requirements.txt
!docker/api/requirements.txt
!docker/ui/requirements.txt

# The cross-encoder, staged by scripts/stage_reranker_model.py. It loads with
# local_files_only=True, so an image without it fails at the first reranked query
# rather than at start-up.
!docker/api/model/

# The CPU-only torch wheel, staged by scripts/stage_build_wheels.py, because its
# index is not verifiable from inside the build. See docker/api/Dockerfile.
!docker/api/wheels/

# Streamlit theme. Committed, contains no configuration and no secret.
!.streamlit/config.toml

# Re-excluded after the re-admissions above, because `!src/` would otherwise pull
# compiled caches from the developer's working tree into the layer.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
